# A new course: `quarto use template insufficientdoubt/project-chalkline` copies this repository
# into a new folder and installs Chalkline (_extensions/) in it. It leaves out what's listed here:
# this sample's own content and Chalkline's planning files. The new course gets its own starter unit
# and course files from `python chalkline.py setup`, which the launchers run the first time.

# Quarto leaves out every dotfile and README.md, CLAUDE.md and AGENTS.md unless told otherwise:
!.*
!README.md
!CLAUDE.md
!AGENTS.md

# Not for a new course
.quartoignore
.github
.git
.venv
.quarto
_site
_site-teacher
_freeze
generated
archive
exports
EXTENSION-PLAN.md
V1-PLAN.md
IDEAS.md
TOOL-CHANGES.md

# The sample's content (the starter's own come from _extensions/chalkline/starter/)
course/units
course/vocab
course/season.yml
course/links.yml
vocab/data
vocab/images
vocab/tools
vocab/app
vocab/schema.yaml
vocab/config.js
